{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The CSV filtering CLI in `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/154-087-cli-parser-bug-tests-atomic-a02-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-087-cli-parser-bug-tests-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-082139-5ff3a6dd/workspace/in/csvtool` has parsing bugs around quoted fields, empty results, and descending sort.\n\nYour job:\n- Run `python -m pytest tests` from `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/154-087-cli-parser-bug-tests-atomic-a02-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-087-cli-parser-bug-tests-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-082139-5ff3a6dd/workspace/in/csvtool`.\n- Fix the CLI implementation.\n- Add focused regression tests for the bug. A good place is `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/154-087-cli-parser-bug-tests-atomic-a02-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-087-cli-parser-bug-tests-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-082139-5ff3a6dd/workspace/in/csvtool/tests/test_cli_regression.py`.\n- Verify the full test suite passes.\n\nRequired CLI behavior:\n- `python -m csvtool.cli samples/orders.csv --where status=paid --select id,total --sort -created_at`\n- Repeating `--where` applies all predicates with AND semantics, for example `--where status=paid --where total=750`.\n- CSV parsing and writing must preserve quoted commas correctly.\n- Empty result sets should still print the selected header and exit 0.\n- `--sort -field` means descending; `--sort field` means ascending. Numeric-looking values should sort numerically.\n- Bad `--where` expressions should exit non-zero with a clear message.\n- Selecting, sorting, or filtering on a missing field should exit non-zero with a clear message.\n\nConstraints:\n- Do not modify existing tests in `tests/test_cli_existing.py`.\n- Do not hard-code sample rows or fixture file paths.\n- Do not introduce pandas, click, or other external dependencies.\n- Do not parse CSV by splitting lines on commas.\n- Do not remove CLI options or bypass filtering.\n"}],"timestamp":1788178925314}}
